/P 932 0 R
/S /Figure
/Alt (The image consists of a visual representation and a caption. Visual representation. A curve and a rectangle are graphed above a horizontal line. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the horizontal line. Two points are labeled on the horizontal line. They are as follows from left to right: a and b. The curve begins at a point vertically above the point a on top left of the viewing window, goes down and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends at the point b on the horizontal line. The region under the curve till the horizontal line is shaded. The left and right boundaries of the shaded region are a and b respectively. The rectangle is graphed between the curve and the horizontal line in the shaded region. The upper side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The lower side of the rectangle lies on the horizontal line. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled R\(x\) and the distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta x. R\(x\) > Delta x. V = pi int_a^b \(\(R\(x\)\)^2\) d x. An arrow points from Delta x to d x in the equation. Caption. Horizontal axis of revolution.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [16]
/Pg 19 0 R
>>
endobj
426 0 obj
<<
/P 932 0 R
/S /Figure
/Alt (The image consists of a visual representation and a caption. Visual representation. A curve and a rectangle are graphed on the right side of a vertical line. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the vertical line. Two points are labeled on the vertical line. They are as follows from bottom to top: c and d. The curve begins at the point d on the vertical line on the top left of the viewing window, goes down and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends at a point horizontally to the right of the point c. The region between the vertical line and the curve is shaded. The bottom and top boundaries of the shaded region are c and d respectively. The rectangle is graphed between the vertical line and the curve in the shaded region. The left side of the rectangle lies on the vertical line. The right side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled R\(x\) and the distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta y. R\(x\) > Delta y. V = pi int_c^d \(\(R\(y\)\)^2\) d y. An arrow points from Delta y to d y in the equation. Caption. Vertical axis of revolution.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [17]
/Pg 19 0 R
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/P 932 0 R
/S /Figure
/Alt (The disk method. To find the volume of a solid of revolution with the disk method, use one of the formulas below. See Figure 7.15. \(item 1\). Horizontal axis of revolution. Volume = V = pi int_a^b \([R\(x\)]^2\) d x. \(item 2\). Vertical axis of revolution. Volume = V = pi int_c^d \([R\(y\)]^2\) d y.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [18]
/Pg 19 0 R
>>
endobj
