/S /Figure
/Alt (Two graphs. \(graph 1\). A curve and a rectangle are graphed in the first quadrant of the x y coordinate plane. The curve is labeled f\(x\) = sqrt\(sin\(x\)\). It begins at the origin, goes up and to the right, reaches a high point at \(pi/2, 1\), then goes down and to the right, and ends at \(pi, 0\) on the positive x axis. The region under the curve till the positive x axis is shaded. The left and right boundaries of the shaded region are x = 0 and x = pi respectively. The shaded region is labeled plane region. The rectangle is graphed between the curve and the positive x axis in the shaded region. The upper side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The lower side of the rectangle lies on the positive x axis. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled R\(x\) and the distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta x. R\(x\) > Delta x. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the x axis. \(graph 2\). A solid of revolution is graphed on the x y coordinate plane in the first and fourth quadrants. The solid of revolution is obtained by revolving the plane region in graph 1 about the x axis. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the x axis.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [66]
/Pg 20 0 R
>>
