/Alt (Two graphs. Each part consists of a visual representation and a caption. \(graph 1\). Visual representation. A shaded region and a rectangle are graphed above a horizontal line. Two points are labeled on the horizontal line. They are as follows from left to right: a and b. The shaded region is bounded by a line and a curve. The line begins at a point vertically above the point a, goes up and to the right, and ends at a point vertically above the point b. The curve begins at the same point as the line begins, goes up and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends at the same point as the line ends. The rectangle is graphed between the line and the curve in the shaded region. The upper side of the rectangle intersects the line. The lower side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The distance between the upper side of the rectangle and the horizontal line is labeled R\(x\). The distance between the lower side of the rectangle and the horizontal line is labeled r\(x\). Caption. Plane region. \(graph 2\). Visual representation. A solid of revolution is graphed around a horizontal line that passes through its center. The solid of revolution is obtained by revolving the plane region in graph 1 about the horizontal line. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the horizontal line. Caption. Solid of revolution with hole.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [4]
/Pg 25 0 R
>>
