/P 946 0 R
/S /Figure
/Alt (The image consists of a visual representation and a caption. Visual representation. A solid is graphed on the x y coordinate plane. The x and y axis are graphed on one horizontal plane. Two points labeled a and b are marked on the x axis. They are placed on either sides of the y axis. The left surface of the solid stretches from point a to point b. The left surface goes up from the x axis perpendicular to it and forms a polygon with four sides resembling a square. A curve from each corner of the polygon goes to the right and ends at a point on the y axis. The base of the solid is in the x y plane. A cross section of the solid, perpendicular to the x axis is marked. The width of the cross-section on the x axis is labeled Delta x. Caption. A. Cross sections perpendicular to x axis.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [2]
/Pg 33 0 R
>>
endobj
