/Alt (The image consists of a visual representation and a caption. Visual representation. A solid resembling a pyramid with three sides is graphed on the x y coordinate plane. The x and y axis are graphed on one horizontal plane. The triangular base of the solid is in the x y plane bounded by three lines. One line is labeled y = f\(x\). It begins at \(0, 1\) on the positive y axis, and ends at \(2, 0\) on the positive x axis. The second line is labeled y = g\(x\). It begins at \(0, negative 1\) on the negative y axis, and ends at \(2, 0\) on the positive x axis. The third line lies on the y axis. It begins at \(0, negative 1\) on the negative y axis, passes through the origin, and ends at \(0, 1\) on the positive y axis. The three sides of the pyramid are the same as the base with one of the sides parallel to the y axis. A cross-section of the solid, perpendicular to the x axis is marked. Caption. Cross sections are equilateral triangles.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [33]
/Pg 34 0 R
>>
