/Alt (Two graphs. \(graph 1\). A right triangle and a rectangle are graphed above a horizontal line. The opposite side of the triangle is a vertical line. It goes up from the point labeled c to the point labeled d. The adjacent side of the triangle is a horizontal line. It goes to the right from the point c and ends. The hypotenuse side of the triangle is a line that goes down and to the right from the point d to the end of the adjacent side. The angle between the adjacent and opposite sides is a right angle. The region bounded by the triangle is shaded and is labeled plane region. The rectangle is graphed in the plane region. The left side of the rectangle lies on the opposite side of the triangle. The right side of the rectangle intersects the hypotenuse side of the triangle. The distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled h\(y\). The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta y. h\(y\) > Delta y. The distance between the center of the rectangle and the horizontal line is labeled p\(y\). \(graph 2\). A solid of revolution is graphed around a horizontal line that passes through its center. The horizontal line is labeled axis of revolution. The solid of revolution is obtained by revolving the plane region in graph 1 about the axis of revolution. The rectangle graphed in the plane region also revolves and generates a solid inside the solid of revolution. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the axis of revolution.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [52]
/Pg 41 0 R
>>
