/S /Figure
/Alt (The shell method. To find the volume of a solid of revolution with the shell method, use one of the formulas below. See Figure 7.29. \(item 1\). Horizontal Axis of Revolution. Volume = V = 2 pi int_c^d \(p\(y\) h\(y\)\) d y. \(item 2\). Vertical Axis of Revolution. Volume = V = 2 pi int_a^b \(p\(x\) h\(x\)\) d x.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [2]
/Pg 43 0 R
>>
endobj
866 0 obj
<<
/P 956 0 R
/S /Figure
/Alt (Two graphs. Each part consists of a visual representation and a caption. \(graph 1\). Visual representation. A curve and a rectangle are graphed above a horizontal line. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the horizontal line. The curve begins at a point labeled d on the top left of the viewing window, goes down and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends above the horizontal line. A point labeled c is marked vertically under the point d and horizontally to the left of the end of the curve. The region bounded by the curve, the vertical line stretching from point d to point c, and the horizontal line stretching from point c to the end of the curve is shaded. The rectangle is graphed in the shaded region. The left side of the rectangle lies on the vertical line stretching from point d to point c. The right side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled h\(y\). The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta y. h\(y\) > Delta y. The distance between the center of the rectangle and the horizontal line is labeled p\(y\). Caption. Horizontal axis of revolution. \(graph 2\). Visual representation. A curve and a rectangle are graphed on the right of a vertical line. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the vertical line. The curve begins at a point on the top left of the viewing window just to the right of the vertical line, goes down and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends at a point labeled b. A point labeled a is marked vertically under the start point of the curve and horizontally to the left of the point b. The region bounded by the curve, the vertical line stretching from the start of the curve to the point a, and the horizontal line stretching from point a to point b is shaded. The rectangle is graphed in the shaded region. The upper side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The lower side of the rectangle lies on the horizontal line stretching from point a to point b. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled h\(x\). The distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta x. h\(x\) > Delta x. The distance between the center of the rectangle and the vertical line is labeled p\(x\). Caption. Vertical axis of revolution.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [3]
/Pg 43 0 R
>>
endobj
