/Alt (A curve and a rectangle are graphed in the first quadrant of the x y coordinate plane. The vertical y axis is labeled axis of revolution. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the y axis. The curve is labeled y = x minus x^3. It begins at the origin, goes up and to the right, reaches a high point, then goes down and to the right, and ends at \(1, 0\) on the positive x axis. The region under the curve till the positive x axis is shaded. The left and right boundaries of the shaded region are x = 0 and x = 1 respectively. The rectangle is graphed between the curve and the positive x axis in the shaded region. The upper side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The lower side of the rectangle lies on the positive x axis. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled h\(x\) = x minus x^3 and the distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta x. h\(x\) > Delta x. The distance between the center of the rectangle and the y axis is labeled p\(x\) = x.)
