/S /Figure
/Alt (Two parts. Each part consists of a caption and two graphs. Each graph consists of a caption and a visual representation \(part 1\). Caption. Disk method: representative rectangle is perpendicular to the axis of revolution. \(graph 1\). Caption. Vertical axis of revolution. Visual representation. A curve and a rectangle are graphed in the first quadrant of the x y coordinate plane. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the y axis. Two points are labeled on the positive y axis. They are as follows from bottom to top: c and d. The curve begins at a point just to the right of the positive y axis for which y = d, goes down and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends at a point just above the positive x axis for which y = c. The region bounded by the curve, the vertical line passing through the start point of the curve, and the horizontal line y = c is shaded. The rectangle is graphed in the shaded region. The left side of the rectangle lies on the vertical line passing through the start point of the curve. The right side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The distance between the positive y axis and the left side of the rectangle is labeled r. The distance between the positive y axis and the right side of the rectangle is labeled R. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta y. R minus r > Delta y. V = pi int_c^d \(R^2 minus r^2\) d y. An arrow points from Delta y to d y in the equation. \(graph 2\). Caption. Horizontal axis of revolution. Visual representation. A curve and a rectangle are graphed in the first quadrant of the x y coordinate plane. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the x axis. Two points are labeled on the positive x axis. They are as follows from left to right: a and b. The curve begins at a point just to the right of the positive y axis for which x = a, goes down and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends at a point just above the positive x axis for which x = b. The region bounded by the curve, the vertical line x = a, and the horizontal line passing through the end point of the curve is shaded. The rectangle is graphed in the shaded region. The upper side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The lower side of the rectangle lies on the horizontal line passing through the end point of the curve. The distance between the upper side of the rectangle and the positive x axis is labeled R. The distance between the lower side of the rectangle and the positive x axis is labeled r. The distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta x. R minus r > Delta x. V = pi int_a^b \(R^2 minus r^2\) d x. An arrow points from Delta x to d x in the equation. \(part 2\). Caption. Shell method: representative rectangle is parallel to the axis of revolution. \(graph 1\). Caption. Vertical axis of revolution. Visual representation. A curve and a rectangle are graphed in the first quadrant of the x y coordinate plane. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the y axis. Two points are labeled on the positive x axis. They are as follows from left to right: a and b. The curve begins at a point just to the right of the positive y axis for which x = a, goes down and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends at a point just above the positive x axis for which x = b. The region bounded by the curve, the vertical line x = a, and the horizontal line passing through the end point of the curve is shaded. The rectangle is graphed in the shaded region. The upper side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The lower side of the rectangle lies on the horizontal line passing through the end point of the curve. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled h. The distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta x. h > Delta x. The distance between the positive y axis and the center of the rectangle is labeled p. V = 2 pi int_a^b \(p h\) d x. An arrow points from Delta x to d x in the equation. \(graph 2\). Caption. Horizontal axis of revolution. Visual representation. A curve and a rectangle are graphed in the first quadrant of the x y coordinate plane. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the x axis. Two points are labeled on the positive y axis. They are as follows from bottom to top: c and d. The curve begins at a point just to the right of the positive y axis for which y = d, goes down and to the right with increasing steepness, and ends at a point just above the positive x axis for which y = c. The region bounded by the curve, the vertical line passing through the start point of the curve, and the horizontal line y = c is shaded. The rectangle is graphed in the shaded region. The left side of the rectangle lies on the vertical line passing through the start point of the curve. The right side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The distance between the left and right sides of the rectangle is labeled h. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta y. h > Delta y. The distance between the center of the rectangle and the positive x axis is labeled p. V = 2 pi int_c^d \(p h\) d y. An arrow points from Delta y to d y in the equation.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [4]
/Pg 46 0 R
>>
endobj
