/Alt (The image consists of a visual representation and a caption. Visual representation. A curve and two rectangles are graphed in the first quadrant of the x y coordinate plane. The vertical y axis is labeled axis of revolution. An arrow indicates a counterclockwise rotation of the y axis. The curve resembles the right half of an upward opening parabola. It begins at \(0, 1\) on the positive y axis, goes up and to the right, and ends at the labeled point \(1, 2\). The region under the curve till the positive x axis is shaded. The left and right boundaries of the shaded region are x = 0 and x = 1 respectively. One rectangle is graphed between the curve and the vertical line x = 1 in the shaded region. The left side of the rectangle intersects the curve. The right side of the rectangle lies on the vertical line x = 1. The distance between the positive y axis and the left side of the rectangle is labeled r. The distance between the positive y axis and the right side of the rectangle is labeled R. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta y. R minus r > Delta y. The second rectangle is graphed under the curve in the shaded region. The left side of the rectangle lies on the positive y axis. The right side of the rectangle lies on the vertical line x = 1. The distance between the upper and lower sides of the rectangle is labeled Delta y. For 1 <= y <= 2: R = 1 and r = sqrt\(y minus 1\). For 0 <= y <= 1: R = 1 and r = 0. Caption. A. Disk method.)
/Type /StructElem
/K [7]
/Pg 47 0 R
>>
